begin{aligned}tan⁡(-a) & =-tan⁡a \\\\  & =-(-3) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["7c773ce7-b806-53fa-ac8d-5fa5adc13bd2"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "735d9684-5834-58d9-8ad9-37bb2fe12482" :answer/id #uuid "735d9684-5834-58d9-8ad9-37bb2fe12482" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "423dd6da-2e83-5a29-8ca3-14205a0d3359" :answer/id #uuid "423dd6da-2e83-5a29-8ca3-14205a0d3359" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "920765f7-8e65-58e0-be2c-82a5a1673a79" :answer/id #uuid "920765f7-8e65-58e0-be2c-82a5a1673a79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "301d3410-ee25-5bb6-aca3-b0a43dac95ef" :answer/id #uuid "301d3410-ee25-5bb6-aca3-b0a43dac95ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "c828bbfd-efc6-53f3-bdce-cb9177bfe7b3" :answer/id #uuid "c828bbfd-efc6-53f3-bdce-cb9177bfe7b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "cfebc5db-f450-59fa-a0c9-e6fce96500f4" :answer-field/id #uuid "cfebc5db-f450-59fa-a0c9-e6fce96500f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["735d9684-5834-58d9-8ad9-37bb2fe12482" "423dd6da-2e83-5a29-8ca3-14205a0d3359" "920765f7-8e65-58e0-be2c-82a5a1673a79" "301d3410-ee25-5bb6-aca3-b0a43dac95ef" "c828bbfd-efc6-53f3-bdce-cb9177bfe7b3"] :answer-field/correct "301d3410-ee25-5bb6-aca3-b0a43dac95ef" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "3a223131-a445-5eaa-af96-514c74007b30" :question/id #uuid "3a223131-a445-5eaa-af96-514c74007b30" :question/problem "If $tan⁡x=6,$ then $tan⁡(-x)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](images/df/df1aba3f5ff980de82a74dde8170ad708e379caf2188873bcddc83177e87c7a6.png)\n\nOur graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. If we rotate the graph ${180}^{∘}$ around the origin, we get the same picture. This means that $tan⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡(-x)=-tan⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡(-x) & =-tan⁡x \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["cfebc5db-f450-59fa-a0c9-e6fce96500f4"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "926faefa-4b6d-5479-8997-673f316ca72d" :answer/id #uuid "926faefa-4b6d-5479-8997-673f316ca72d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2} - 4π" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "3d5985b1-90fb-523b-bdad-f972630acc1c" :answer/id #uuid "3d5985b1-90fb-523b-bdad-f972630acc1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "a4be77bc-5e7d-55e6-a876-3536000cf35f" :answer/id #uuid "a4be77bc-5e7d-55e6-a876-3536000cf35f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e4a0729f-1ad9-5069-84c1-ad7734a10d53" :answer/id #uuid "e4a0729f-1ad9-5069-84c1-ad7734a10d53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e7e20b13-6e2d-5031-8a95-abaaee22c4fa" :answer/id #uuid "e7e20b13-6e2d-5031-8a95-abaaee22c4fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2} - 4π" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "3516c524-2cbd-5e56-944a-25c46fe63015" :answer-field/id #uuid "3516c524-2cbd-5e56-944a-25c46fe63015" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["926faefa-4b6d-5479-8997-673f316ca72d" "3d5985b1-90fb-523b-bdad-f972630acc1c" "a4be77bc-5e7d-55e6-a876-3536000cf35f" "e4a0729f-1ad9-5069-84c1-ad7734a10d53" "e7e20b13-6e2d-5031-8a95-abaaee22c4fa"] :answer-field/correct "e4a0729f-1ad9-5069-84c1-ad7734a10d53" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "399cc078-de71-5c47-b032-5dcccc702272" :question/id #uuid "399cc078-de71-5c47-b032-5dcccc702272" :question/problem "If $\\tan x = \\frac{3}{2}$, then $\\tan (-x - 4π) =$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](images/df/df1aba3f5ff980de82a74dde8170ad708e379caf2188873bcddc83177e87c7a6.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note the following:\n\n- The period of $tan⁡x$ is $\\pi .$\n\n- Our graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. This means that $tan⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡(-x)=-tan⁡x.\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate our expression:\n\n- Firstly, using the periodicity of $tan⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡(-x-4\\pi ) & =tan⁡(-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Secondly, using the oddness of $tan⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡(-x) & =-tan⁡x \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\tan (-x - 4π)=-\\frac{3}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["3516c524-2cbd-5e56-944a-25c46fe63015"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "3bbbdfef-ff18-5840-a720-bf3a6e3607ad" :answer/id #uuid "3bbbdfef-ff18-5840-a720-bf3a6e3607ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4} + 6π" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "a1c4bac2-ad78-587b-af3a-667ee44fb5ee" :answer/id #uuid "a1c4bac2-ad78-587b-af3a-667ee44fb5ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{4}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "deab0bda-34c3-53e6-babc-d4b07ef2a1d2" :answer/id #uuid "deab0bda-34c3-53e6-babc-d4b07ef2a1d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{4} + 6π" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "d814092d-bfbb-5323-a7b1-522b7df39eff" :answer/id #uuid "d814092d-bfbb-5323-a7b1-522b7df39eff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "543421b3-6f98-5b39-8bf2-a75be506ac0b" :answer/id #uuid "543421b3-6f98-5b39-8bf2-a75be506ac0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f15360d1-03e2-5d57-9abe-a5cfabf7bc07" :answer-field/id #uuid "f15360d1-03